## Triage correction

The accepted [subject-only decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) is historical evidence, not reliable current guidance. Its accepted text remains unchanged. [Decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause) proposes its replacement: merge only when the cause is established as the same. Equal subjects can conceal different bugs; different subjects can describe the same bug. Missing tenant evidence means hold for review, not automatic merge.

<DedupeExplorer />

## Verification and keeping this page current

For each fix, test ambiguous dates (for example 03/04), unambiguous days above 12, and the tenant locales and input paths listed above. Check expected booking and invite dates end to end; a changed hint or unit parser result alone is insufficient. Investigate the anomalous reports with original timestamps and timezone details without asserting an unsupported third root cause.

Counts are computed from unique IDs and tenant records by the supplied components. Rebuild after every desk export or tenant-directory change, reconcile totals, and inspect this rendered page before using it. Continue recording receivedAt separately from mergedAt. A growing queue or a new merge batch is not evidence that an old cause has disappeared.

Sources: `src/lib/data/reports-4471.json`, `src/lib/data/tenants/*.json`, `src/lib/data/desk-notes.json`, `src/lib/kb/causes.ts`, `locales.ts`, `CauseTable.svelte`, `QueueTimeline.svelte`, `DedupeExplorer.svelte` and decision 0001.

